      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "PURPOSE",
          "content": "We studied the effect of myocardial ischemia and diabetes mellitus (DM) on the myocardial fatty acid metabolism using 123I-BMIPP myocardial scintigraphy."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "We performed 123I-BMIPP myocardial scintigraphy in 50 patients with myocardial ischemia and without DM (AP), in 30 patients with myocardial ischemia and DM (AP + DM), 12 patients with DM and without myocardial ischemia (DM), and in 10 normal subjects (N). Myocardial uptake rate of 123I-BMIPP was obtained using the time activity curve. Myocardial washout rate of 123I-BMIPP was calculated using the polar images of early and delayed SPECT images."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Myocardial uptake rate of 123I-BMIPP (%) were AP: 4.9 +/- 0.6, AP + DM: 5.5 +/- 0.5, DM 5.7 +/- 0.5 and N: 5.0 +/- 0.4. 123I-BMIPP myocardial uptake rate was increased in AP + DM and DM. 123I-BMIPP myocardial washout rate (%) were AP: 30.2 +/- 4.3, AP + DM: 24.5 +/- 3.9, DM: 16.1 +/- 2.8 and N: 19.4 +/- 3.2. 123I-BMIPP myocardial washout rate was increased in AP and AP + DM. 123I-BMIPP myocardial washout rate was increased particularly in patients with multi-vessels disease. 123I-BMIPP myocardial washout rate was decreased in DM."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "The present study suggested that diabetes mellitus increased myocardial fatty acid uptake and decreased myocardial fatty acid washout, and that myocardial ischemia increased myocardial fatty acid washout."
        }
      ]},
